Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:43:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] SQL Server connections: .NET Framework's Encrypt
 default

The runtime's SQL Server components (membership, roles, profile, session state,
SqlDataSource, cache dependencies, web events) use Microsoft.Data.SqlClient where .NET
Framework used System.Data.SqlClient. The applications' connection strings were
written for the latter, whose Encrypt was false unless set; Microsoft.Data.SqlClient's
is true, and the connection fails against a server with its own certificate (SQL
Server Express): DNN's install could not create its administrator. A connection string
that does not say gets Encrypt=False.
